{"id":"word:hebrew:H3678","type":"word","title":"כִּסֵּא","subtitle":"H3678 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"properly, covered , i.e. a throne (as canopied )","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to כִּסֵּא (H3678) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 135 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"כִּסֵּא (kiççêʼ) means properly, covered , i.e. a throne (as canopied ) First listed occurrence: 1Chr 17 12."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"כִּסֵּא","transliteration":"kiççêʼ","pronunciation":"kis-say'","strong":"H3678","lemmaId":"hebrew:H3678","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["כִּסֵּ֣א","כִּסֵּ֥א","כִּסְא֔/וֹ","כִּסְא֜/וֹ","כִּסְא֑/וֹ"],"morphs":[["HNcmsc",43],["HNcmsc/Sp3ms",31],["HNcmsc/Sp1cs",10],["HNcmsa",10],["HNcmsc/Sp2ms",7],["HTd/Ncmsa",7],["HC/Ncmsc/Sp3ms",5],["HRd/Ncmsa",5],["HR/Ncmsc",4],["HR/Ncmsa",3]]},"definitions":{"short":"properly, covered , i.e. a throne (as canopied )","usage":"seat, stool, throne.","full":"H3678. kisse or kisseh כִּסֵּה כִּסֵּא, 133 noun masculine 2Sam 7:16 seat of honour, throne (Late Hebrew id. ; Phoenician (plural) כרסים ; Aramaic כּוּרְסְיָא , ; Biblical Aramaic כָּרְסֵא , Zinjirli כרסא DHM Sendsch. 58. 44 ; Arabic ; but Assyrian kussu ; perhaps Akkadian loan-word; ideogram iƒ GU. ZA , compare Dl HWB 343 ); — absolute כִּסֵּא Gen 41:40 +; כִּסֵּת 1Kin 10:19 (twice in verse); Job 26:9 , הַכִּסֶּא Ezek 1:26 ; construct כִּסֵּא 2Sam 3:10 +, כֵּס Exod 17:16 (si vera lectio; see below); suffix כִּסְאִי 1Kin 1:13 +, כִּסְאֲךָ 2Sam 7:16 +, כִּסְאֶ֑ךָ 1 Kings 5:19 +, כִּסְאוֺ Exod 11:5 +; plural כִּסְאוֺת Psa 122:5 (twice in verse); suffix כִּסְאוֺתָם Ezek 26:16 ; Isa 14:9 ; &#8212; seat of honour , usually 1. a. of king = throne Gen 41:40 (E), Exod 11:5 ; 12:29 (both J) 1Kin 2:19 ; Isa 47:1 ; Ezek 26:16 ; of queen-mother 1Kin 2:19 b; ׳כ מַלְכוּתוֺ Est 5:1 his royal throne ; of future (Messianic) prince Zech 6:13 a (in v b read ᵐ5 עליֿמינו Sta ZAW 1881, 10 ); of dead kings in She'ôl Isa 14:9 ; כ ׳נָתַן , in, or against a place, said of king himself, (only Jeremiah) is a sign of conquest ( Jer 1:15 ); so כּ ׳שִׂים 43:10 , and (of ׳י ) 49:38 ; in Judg 3:20 , though of king, not seat of office; 12t. elsewhere, literal b. throne of ׳י ( אלהים ) as heavenly king, Isa 6:1 ; Ezek 1:26 (twice in verse); 10:1 ; 1Kin 22:19 2Chr 18:18 ; Job 26:9 ; Psa 11:4 ; Isa 66:1 heaven is my throne ; as seat of judgment Psa 9:5 ; 9:8 ; in oath יָהּ עַלכּכֵּס יָד Exod 17:16 (compare Di; &gt; Cler JDMich Ges Buhl SS נֵס banner ; ᵐ5 κρυφαία √ כסה , favours כס ); Jerusalem called throne of ׳י Jer 3:17 , so the sanctuary 17:12 ( ׳כ מָרוֺם כָּבוֺד ), Ezek 43:7 . 2 of high priest 1Sam 1:9 ; 4:13 , 18 ; of honoured guest 2Kin 4:10 ; of governor Neh 3:7 ; of (unjust) judge ׳כ הַוּוֺת Psa 94:20 ; = conspicuous seat (literally) Prov 9:14 ; = seat of distinction, explicitly ׳כ כָּבוֺד Isa 22:23 ; ׳כ alone 2Kin 25:28 (twice in verse) = Jer 52:32 (twice in verse); Est 3:1 . 3. a. figurative = royal dignity, authority, power , נָקִי וְכִסְאוֺ הַמֶּלֶךְ 2Sam 14:9 ; וּלְכ וּלְבֵיתוֺ וּלְזַרְעוֺ ׳לְדָוִד 1Kin 2:33 ; especially kingdom , with verbs of setting up, establishing , ׳י subject, כ ׳הֵקִים דָוִד 2Sam 3:10 , כִסְאֲךָוּבָנִיתִי Psa 89:5 , so with שִׂים 89:30 ; king subject, כִּסְאוֺסָעַד בַּחֶסֶד Prov 20:28 ; passive ׳כ נכִון יִהְיֶה דָוִד 1Kin 2:45 the throne of David shall be established , compare 2Sam 7:16 = 1Chr 17:14 ; כ בַּחֶסֶד ׳וְהוּכַן Isa 16:5 (of Messianic reign); so (in General) כ יִכּוֺן ׳בִּצְדָקָה Prov 16:12 , compare 25:5 ; 29:14 ; intransitive (with הָיָה ) Psa 89:37 ; more fully, ׳י subject, אֶתכֿ ׳וְכֹנַנְתִּי מַמְלַכְתּוֺ 2Sam 7:13 ( כסאו כֹּנֵן in || 1Chr 17:12 ), אֶתכֿ ׳יִשְׂרָאֵלוַהֲקִמֹתִי עַֿ מַמְלַכְתְּךָ 1Kin 9:5 , compare || 2Chr 7:18 and כ ׳וַהֲכִינוֺתִי &lt;Times New Roman&gt; עַליִֿשְׂרָאֵל מַלְכוּתוֺ 1Chr 22:10 ; also כ ׳מגּר Psa 89:45 cast down throne , of Gentile nations כ ׳מַמְלָכוֺתוְהָפַכְתִּי Hag 2:22 ; עלכֿ ׳יָשַׁב sit on the throne of any one (especially David) = be his successor 1Kin 1:13 , 17 , 20 , 24 , 27 , 30 , 35 , 48 ; 2:12 ; 3:6 ; 2Kin 13:13 , especially Jer 13:13 ; 17:25 ; 22:2 5 t. Jeremiah; לְכ ׳ֵישְׁבוּ לָ֑ךְ Psa 132:12 ; more fully 1Chr 29:23 ; causative עלכֿ ׳הוֺשִׁיב 1Kin 2:24 ; 1 Kings 5:19; 2Kin 10:3 ; לַכּ ׳הֹשִׁיב figurative Job 36:7 , of placing in honour; לְכ אָשִׁית בִטְנְךָ ׳מִמְּרִי לָ֑ךְ Psa 132:11 ; ישׁב׳עלכֿ also = take one's seat as king, become actual king, possess royalty 1Kin 16:11 , often sit on the throne of Israel 8:20 , 25 2Chr 6:10 , 16 ; 1Kin 10:9 ; 2Kin 10:30 ; 15:12 ; Jer 33:17 ; without ישׁב 1Kin 2:4 ; 9:5 , compare also Isa 9:6 (Messiah); מַמְלַכְתּוֺ עלכֿסא ישׁב Deut 17:18 , הַמְּלוּכָה עלכֿסא 1Kin 1:46 , and even י מַלְכוּת ׳עַלכִּֿסֵּא עַליִֿשְׂרָאֵללָשֶׁבֶת 1Chr 28:5 ; also ׳עַלכֿ ישׁב הַמְּלָכִים 2Kin 11:19 , || ׳כ הַמַּמְלָכָה 2Chron 23:30; of (royal) throne as judgment seat Prov 20:8 , compare also Psa 122:5 ; set one upon the throne of Israel פ ׳נתן ׳עלכֿ ׳ישׂ 1Kin 10:9 compare || 2Chr 9:8 ; in comparative sentence מִכּ אֶתכִּֿסְאוֺ ׳יְגַדֵּל , i.e. make him a more powerful king than, 1Kin 1:37 , compare 1:47 ; of king of Babylon, כִּסְאִי אָרִים לְכוֺכְבֵיאֵֿל מִמַּעַל Isa 14:13 . In Psa 45:7 וגו אלהים ׳כִּסְאֲךָ the text is probably corrupt: AE Hi Ew Bae read thy throne is ( a throne ) of God ; Bi Che insert יסודתו הקימונכונה thy throne [ its foundation is firmly fixed ], God [has established it]; see further Dr § 194, Obs.. b. throne of י ׳(אלהים) = his royal dignity, sovereign, Lam 5:19 ; Psa 93:2 ; 103:19 ( כ ׳הֵכִין ; || מַלְכוּת ); ׳כ כְבוֺדֶ֑ךָ Jer 14:21 ; עַלכֿ ׳יָשַׁב קָדְשׁוֺ Psa 47:9 ; כִּסְאֶ֑ךָ מְכוֺן וּמִשְׁמָּט צֶדֶק 89:15 ; compare 97:2 . כסא (see Biblical Hebrew כִּסֵּא throne ).","rootNote":"or כִּסֵּה ; from 3680 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 17 12","keyReferences":["1Chr 17 12","1Chr 1